<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="utf-8"/>
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1"/>
  <title>cvprofiles report — {{ run_id[:12] }}</title>
  <style>
    :root {
      --ink: #1a1410;
      --muted: #5c534c;
      --paper: #f7f1e8;
      --card: #fffdf8;
      --line: #d9cfc0;
      --ok: #1f6b3a;
      --bad: #8b1e1e;
      --accent: #6b2c2c;
      --chip: #efe6d8;
    }
    * { box-sizing: border-box; }
    body {
      margin: 0;
      font-family: "Iowan Old Style", "Palatino Linotype", Palatino, Georgia, serif;
      color: var(--ink);
      background: var(--paper);
      line-height: 1.45;
    }
    .wrap { max-width: 920px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 2rem 1.25rem 3rem; }
    header {
      border-bottom: 2px solid var(--accent);
      padding-bottom: 1rem;
      margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
    }
    .eyebrow {
      font-family: Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif;
      font-size: 0.75rem;
      letter-spacing: 0.08em;
      text-transform: uppercase;
      color: var(--accent);
      margin: 0 0 0.35rem;
    }
    h1 { font-size: 1.75rem; margin: 0 0 0.35rem; font-weight: 600; }
    .sub { color: var(--muted); margin: 0; font-size: 0.98rem; }
    .grid { display: grid; gap: 1rem; grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
    @media (min-width: 760px) {
      .grid.two { grid-template-columns: 1.1fr 0.9fr; }
    }
    .card {
      background: var(--card);
      border: 1px solid var(--line);
      border-radius: 10px;
      padding: 1rem 1.1rem;
    }
    h2 {
      font-size: 1.05rem;
      margin: 0 0 0.75rem;
      font-family: Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif;
      letter-spacing: 0.02em;
    }
    .range-box {
      border-left: 4px solid {% if empty %}var(--bad){% else %}var(--ok){% endif %};
      padding: 0.85rem 1rem;
      background: {% if empty %}#f8ecec{% else %}#eef6f0{% endif %};
      border-radius: 0 8px 8px 0;
      margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
    }
    .range-box .label {
      font-family: Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif;
      font-size: 0.72rem;
      text-transform: uppercase;
      letter-spacing: 0.07em;
      color: var(--muted);
      margin: 0 0 0.25rem;
    }
    .range-box .value {
      font-size: 1.45rem;
      font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
      margin: 0;
    }
    .muted { color: var(--muted); font-size: 0.92rem; }
    table {
      width: 100%;
      border-collapse: collapse;
      font-size: 0.92rem;
      font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
    }
    th, td {
      border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line);
      padding: 0.45rem 0.35rem;
      text-align: left;
      vertical-align: top;
    }
    th {
      font-family: Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif;
      font-size: 0.72rem;
      text-transform: uppercase;
      letter-spacing: 0.05em;
      color: var(--muted);
      font-weight: 600;
    }
    .tag {
      display: inline-block;
      font-family: Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif;
      font-size: 0.72rem;
      padding: 0.12rem 0.45rem;
      border-radius: 999px;
      background: var(--chip);
    }
    .tag.ok { background: #d9eedf; color: var(--ok); }
    .tag.bad { background: #f0d6d6; color: var(--bad); }
    .tag.empty { background: #f0d6d6; color: var(--bad); }
    .mono {
      font-family: ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, Menlo, Consolas, monospace;
      font-size: 0.82rem;
      word-break: break-all;
    }
    ul.compact { margin: 0.25rem 0 0; padding-left: 1.1rem; }
    footer {
      margin-top: 1.75rem;
      padding-top: 0.85rem;
      border-top: 1px solid var(--line);
      color: var(--muted);
      font-size: 0.85rem;
      font-family: Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif;
    }
    .empty-callout {
      border: 1px solid #e0b4b4;
      background: #fbf1f1;
      border-radius: 10px;
      padding: 1rem 1.1rem;
      margin: 0.5rem 0 1rem;
    }
    .empty-callout h2 { color: var(--bad); margin-bottom: 0.4rem; }
  </style>
</head>
<body>
  <div class="wrap">
    <header>
      <p class="eyebrow">cvprofiles · construct-validity profile</p>
      <h1>{{ title }}</h1>
      <p class="sub">
        Admissible measurement set under a stated nomological network, and the
        image of <em>β</em> on that set. Empty sets and wide ranges are scientific features.
      </p>
    </header>

    {% if empty %}
    <section class="empty-callout">
      <h2>Empty admissible set — success, not a crash</h2>
      <p style="margin:0">
        Under this network and thresholds, <strong>no candidate measure survives</strong>.
        The engine is not broken: the theory + data reject the whole menu.
        Reported range is undefined; do not auto-loosen θ.
      </p>
    </section>
    {% endif %}

    <div class="grid two">
      <section class="card">
        <h2>Construct-identified range</h2>
        <div class="range-box">
          <p class="label">[L, U] · method = min/max B*</p>
          {% if empty %}
          <p class="value">∅ &nbsp;<span class="tag empty">empty M*</span></p>
          <p class="muted" style="margin:0.4rem 0 0">No survivors → no image of β. Inference diagnostics are additive and never loosen θ.</p>
          {% else %}
          <p class="value">[{{ "%.6f"|format(L) }}, {{ "%.6f"|format(U) }}]</p>
          <p class="muted" style="margin:0.4rem 0 0">
            Width = {{ "%.6f"|format(U - L) }}
            · {{ "point-ID" if point_id else (admissible|length)|string + " survivors" }}
            {% if bootstrap %}
            {% if bootstrap.band_L is not none and bootstrap.band_U is not none %}
            · bootstrap percentile band = [{{ "%.6f"|format(bootstrap.band_L) }}, {{ "%.6f"|format(bootstrap.band_U) }}]
            {% else %}
            · bootstrap band = ∅ (no non-empty replicates)
            {% endif %}
            {% else %}
            · bootstrap: off
            {% endif %}
          </p>
          {% endif %}
        </div>
        <p class="muted" style="margin:0">
          Target β = <span class="mono">{{ beta_type }}</span>
          on outcome <span class="mono">{{ outcome }}</span>.
          Range uses <strong>only</strong> measures in M*; rejected β values are shown below but never enter [L,U].
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="card">
        <h2>Run freeze</h2>
        <table>
          <tr><th>run_id</th><td class="mono">{{ run_id }}</td></tr>
          <tr><th>package</th><td class="mono">{{ package_version }}</td></tr>
          <tr><th>scores_hash</th><td class="mono">{{ scores_hash }}</td></tr>
          <tr><th>network_hash</th><td class="mono">{{ network_hash }}</td></tr>
          <tr><th>beta_hash</th><td class="mono">{{ beta_hash }}</td></tr>
          <tr><th>δ</th><td class="mono">{{ delta }}</td></tr>
          <tr><th>seed</th><td class="mono">{{ seed }}</td></tr>
          <tr><th>network</th><td>{{ network_name or "—" }}</td></tr>
        </table>
      </section>
    </div>

    {% if bootstrap %}
    <section class="card" style="margin-top:1rem">
      <h2>Bootstrap inference · additive to headline range</h2>
      <p class="muted" style="margin-top:0">
        Units-only Efron resampling; percentile band over non-empty replicates.
        The headline [L, U] above remains min/max β(M*) on the full sample.
      </p>
      <table>
        <tr><th>replicates</th><td>{{ bootstrap.n_boot }}</td></tr>
        <tr><th>seed</th><td>{{ bootstrap.seed }}</td></tr>
        <tr><th>quantiles</th><td>{{ bootstrap.quantiles }}</td></tr>
        <tr><th>non-empty</th><td>{{ bootstrap.replicates_nonempty }}</td></tr>
        <tr><th>empty</th><td>{{ bootstrap.replicates_empty }} ({{ "%.3f"|format(bootstrap.empty_replicate_rate) }})</td></tr>
        <tr><th>degenerate</th><td>{{ bootstrap.replicates_degenerate }} ({{ "%.3f"|format(bootstrap.degenerate_replicate_rate) }})</td></tr>
        <tr><th>band</th><td>{% if bootstrap.band_L is not none and bootstrap.band_U is not none %}[{{ "%.6f"|format(bootstrap.band_L) }}, {{ "%.6f"|format(bootstrap.band_U) }}]{% else %}∅{% endif %}</td></tr>
      </table>
      {% if bootstrap.note %}<p class="muted" style="margin-bottom:0">{{ bootstrap.note }}</p>{% endif %}
    </section>
    {% endif %}

    {% if coverage %}
    <section class="card" style="margin-top:1rem">
      <h2>Uncertainty band · additive to headline range</h2>
      <p class="muted" style="margin-top:0">
        Per-side α/2 quantiles over non-empty bootstrap replicates (α = {{ coverage.alpha }}).
        Heuristic band — <strong>not a confidence interval</strong>, not a holdout-robustness band.
        The headline [L, U] above remains min/max β(M*) on the full sample.
      </p>
      <table>
        <tr><th>α</th><td>{{ coverage.alpha }}</td></tr>
        <tr><th>κ</th><td>{{ coverage.kappa }}</td></tr>
        <tr><th>quantiles</th><td>{{ coverage.quantiles }}</td></tr>
        <tr><th>band</th><td>{% if coverage.band_L is not none and coverage.band_U is not none %}[{{ "%.6f"|format(coverage.band_L) }}, {{ "%.6f"|format(coverage.band_U) }}]{% else %}∅{% endif %}</td></tr>
        <tr><th>empty rate</th><td>{{ "%.3f"|format(coverage.empty_replicate_rate) }}</td></tr>
        <tr><th>degenerate rate</th><td>{{ "%.3f"|format(coverage.degenerate_replicate_rate) }}</td></tr>
      </table>
      {% if coverage.boundary %}
      <h3 style="margin:1rem 0 0.4rem">Boundary attribution · |margin| ≤ κ·SE</h3>
      <table>
        <thead><tr><th>measure</th><th>margin</th><th>SE</th><th>boundary</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          {% for row in coverage.boundary %}
          <tr>
            <td class="mono">{{ row.measure }}</td>
            <td>{{ "%.6f"|format(row.margin) }}</td>
            <td>{% if row.se is not none %}{{ "%.6f"|format(row.se) }}{% else %}—{% endif %}</td>
            <td>{{ "yes" if row.boundary else "no" }}</td>
          </tr>
          {% endfor %}
        </tbody>
      </table>
      {% endif %}
      <h3 style="margin:1rem 0 0.4rem">Admission frequency p̂<sub>m</sub></h3>
      <table>
        <thead><tr><th>measure</th><th>p̂<sub>m</sub></th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          {% for m in measures %}
          <tr>
            <td class="mono">{{ m }}</td>
            <td>{% if coverage.p_hat_m[m] is not none %}{{ "%.3f"|format(coverage.p_hat_m[m]) }}{% else %}—{% endif %}</td>
          </tr>
          {% endfor %}
        </tbody>
      </table>
      {% if coverage.note %}<p class="muted" style="margin-bottom:0">{{ coverage.note }}</p>{% endif %}
    </section>
    {% endif %}

    {% if theta_grid %}
    <section class="card" style="margin-top:1rem">
      <h2>θ-grid sensitivity · diagnostic viewport</h2>
      <p class="muted" style="margin-top:0">
        λ scales threshold magnitudes only. λ is never auto-selected; the headline is always λ=1.0.
        This grid is not part of the freeze preimage.
      </p>
      <table>
        <thead><tr><th>λ</th><th>|M*|</th><th>empty</th><th>L</th><th>U</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          {% for row in theta_grid.rows %}
          <tr>
            <td>{{ row["lambda"] }}</td>
            <td>{{ row.n_admissible }}</td>
            <td>{{ "yes" if row.empty else "no" }}</td>
            <td>{% if row.L is not none %}{{ "%.6f"|format(row.L) }}{% else %}—{% endif %}</td>
            <td>{% if row.U is not none %}{{ "%.6f"|format(row.U) }}{% else %}—{% endif %}</td>
          </tr>
          {% endfor %}
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </section>
    {% endif %}

    {% if delta_grid %}
    <section class="card" style="margin-top:1rem">
      <h2>δ-grid tolerance · diagnostic viewport</h2>
      <p class="muted" style="margin-top:0">
        Absolute tolerance values; δ is never auto-selected. The headline is always the declared δ
        ({{ delta_grid.headline_delta }}). This grid is not part of the freeze preimage.
      </p>
      <table>
        <thead><tr><th>δ</th><th>|M*|</th><th>empty</th><th>L</th><th>U</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          {% for row in delta_grid.rows %}
          <tr>
            <td>{{ row["delta"] }}</td>
            <td>{{ row.n_admissible }}</td>
            <td>{{ "yes" if row.empty else "no" }}</td>
            <td>{% if row.L is not none %}{{ "%.6f"|format(row.L) }}{% else %}—{% endif %}</td>
            <td>{% if row.U is not none %}{{ "%.6f"|format(row.U) }}{% else %}—{% endif %}</td>
          </tr>
          {% endfor %}
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </section>
    {% endif %}

    {% if anchors %}
    <section class="card" style="margin-top:1rem">
      <h2>θ-anchors · pre-data audit</h2>
      <p class="muted" style="margin-top:0">
        One pre-data anchor per restriction (hash <span class="mono">{{ anchors.anchors_hash[:12] }}…</span>).
        The engine enforces completeness + hash; "pre-data" is a process commitment, not a temporal claim.
      </p>
      <table>
        <thead><tr><th>restriction</th><th>kind</th><th>pre-data</th><th>anchor</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          {% for a in anchors.anchors %}
          <tr>
            <td class="mono">{{ a.restriction_id }}</td>
            <td>{{ a.anchor_kind }}</td>
            <td>{{ "yes" if a.pre_data else "no" }}</td>
            <td>{{ a.citation_key }} — {{ a.source_phrase }}</td>
          </tr>
          {% endfor %}
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </section>
    {% endif %}

    <section class="card" style="margin-top:1rem">
      <h2>Menu admission</h2>
      <p class="muted" style="margin-top:0">
        M* size = {{ admissible|length }} / {{ measures|length }}.
        Slack rule: admit if s<sub>r</sub>(m) ≥ −δ for all r.
      </p>
      <table>
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th>measure</th>
            <th>status</th>
            <th>β(m)</th>
            <th>failed restrictions</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          {% for m in measures %}
          <tr>
            <td class="mono">{{ m }}</td>
            <td>
              {% if m in admissible %}
              <span class="tag ok">admissible</span>
              {% else %}
              <span class="tag bad">rejected</span>
              {% endif %}
            </td>
            <td>{{ "%.6f"|format(beta_values[m]) }}</td>
            <td class="mono">
              {% if m in rejected and rejected[m] %}
                {{ rejected[m]|join(", ") }}
              {% else %}
                —
              {% endif %}
            </td>
          </tr>
          {% endfor %}
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </section>

    <section class="card" style="margin-top:1rem">
      <h2>Slack matrix s<sub>r</sub>(m)</h2>
      <p class="muted" style="margin-top:0">Positive / zero ≈ satisfied at δ={{ delta }}. Negative = violation magnitude.</p>
      <table>
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th>measure</th>
            {% for rid in restriction_ids %}
            <th class="mono">{{ rid }}</th>
            {% endfor %}
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          {% for m in measures %}
          <tr>
            <td class="mono">{{ m }}</td>
            {% for rid in restriction_ids %}
            <td>{{ "%.6f"|format(slacks[m][rid]) }}</td>
            {% endfor %}
          </tr>
          {% endfor %}
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </section>

    <section class="card" style="margin-top:1rem">
      <h2>Network (researcher-owned)</h2>
      <ul class="compact">
        {% for r in restrictions %}
        <li>
          <span class="mono">{{ r.id }}</span>
          · type <span class="mono">{{ r.type }}</span>
          · θ={{ r.theta }}
          · params <span class="mono">{{ r.params }}</span>
        </li>
        {% endfor %}
      </ul>
      <p class="muted" style="margin:0.75rem 0 0">
        Engine does not invent restrictions. Agent may author oracle R for synthetic DGPs only.
      </p>
    </section>

    <footer>
      cvprofiles {{ package_version }}
      · four-state spine SCORE → RESTRICT → IDENTIFY → REPORT
      · v1.1/v2.0 inference: bootstrap + θ-grid + δ-grid + coverage (diagnostic)
      · generated {{ created_at or "—" }}
    </footer>
  </div>
</body>
</html>
